# 5. Rock Typing & Permeability Modeling

### 5.1 Hydraulic Flow Units (FZI / DRT) & Permeability Transforms

Rock typing and continuous permeability ($K$) prediction were established using **{{ rt_summary.basis if rt_summary else 'Routine Core Analysis (RCA) & Log-Derived Hydraulic Flow Units' }}** via the Reservoir Quality Index ($RQI$), Normalized Porosity ($\phi_z$), Flow Zone Indicator ($FZI$), and Discrete Rock Typing ($DRT$) formulation:

$$RQI = 0.0314 \sqrt{\frac{K}{\phi_e}}, \quad \phi_z = \frac{\phi_e}{1 - \phi_e}, \quad FZI = \frac{RQI}{\phi_z}, \quad DRT = \text{round}(2 \ln(FZI) + 10.6)$$

